## 2. Inputs, preconditions, and tool contract

### 2.1 Inputs

| Field | Required | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `repo_url` or `repo_id` | yes | — | Single-repo mode |
| `repo_batch` | no | — | CSV/list for batch mode; mutually exclusive with `repo_id` |
| `branch` | no | resolved | See §2.2 |
| `subpaths` | no | `["."]` | Restrict scan to modules, e.g. `["services/payments"]` |
| `include_generated` | no | `false` | Include generated/vendored test dirs |
| `llm_budget` | no | `0` | Max ambiguity-resolution model calls per repo |
| `report_artifacts` | no | `[]` | Paths/URIs to surefire XML, Playwright JSON, Karate JSON, JUnit XML |
| `schema_version` | injected | `1` | Written to every document |

### 2.2 Branch discovery (do not assume `main`)

Resolve in this order, stopping at first success, and record `branch_resolution` in the output:

1. Explicit `branch` input.
2. Repository default branch from the SCM API.
3. First existing of `main`, `master`, `develop`, `trunk`.
4. If none resolve → fail the repo with `RESOLUTION_FAILED`. Do not scan a detached or arbitrary ref silently.

Capture `source_commit` (full 40-char SHA) at resolution time. Every downstream document carries it. If the SHA cannot be captured, abort — idempotency depends on it (§5.4).

### 2.3 Tool contract

Assumed Codemind tool names; rename to match the local registry but preserve the semantics.

| Capability | Tool | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| List files by glob | `repo.list_files(globs, excludes)` | Candidate discovery |
| Read file (ranged) | `repo.read_file(path, start?, end?)` | Signal extraction |
| AST / symbol query | `graphifyy.query(repo, query)` | Java/TS/Python test-unit extraction, import edges |
| Build config parse | `repo.read_file` on POM/Gradle/package.json | Surefire/Failsafe/Playwright projects |
| CI config discovery | `repo.list_files` on CI globs | Gating role (§3.4) |
| Persist | `mongo.upsert(collection, key, doc)` | Idempotent write |

**Degradation rule:** if `graphifyy.query` is unavailable or returns no graph for the repo, fall back to regex-based extraction and set `extraction_mode: "textual"` on every affected record. Textual mode is permitted but must be visible — never present a regex-derived count as if it were AST-derived.

